@startuml c4-containers
!pragma layout smetana
!include theme.iuml
title C4 Level 2: platform applications and data stores
rectangle "User\n[Person]\nLearner or module developer" as User #D5E9EF
rectangle "Training + artifact services\n[External systems]\nGit, registries and dependencies" as Source #EEEEEE
rectangle "EOAP learning and validation platform\n[System boundary; logical applications, not Kubernetes pods]" {
  rectangle "Deployment and acceptance CLI\n[Container: Task + Skaffold + kubectl]\nInstalls services; orchestrates checks" as CLI
  rectangle "Initialization CLI\n[Container: Bash + uv + Git]\nPrepares source, dependencies and kernels" as Init
  rectangle "Learning workspace\n[Container: code-server + Python tooling]\nInteractive editor and exercise execution" as Workspace
  database "Workspace files\n[Container: filesystem on workspace PVC]\nSource, environments and notebook evidence" as Files
  rectangle "Workflow application execution\n[Containers: application images]\nRuns Calrissian-submitted task processes" as Tasks
  database "Shared workflow files\n[Container: filesystem on Calrissian PVC]\nTask inputs, outputs and logs" as Shared
  database "Exercise object store\n[Container: SeaweedFS S3]\nPer-module results; disposable storage" as S3
  rectangle "Optional distributed execution\n[Containers: Dask Gateway + scheduler + workers]\nRuns distributed computation" as Dask
}
User --> CLI : host commands
User --> Workspace : browser via local HTTP forwarding
CLI --> Init : deploys and checks startup\nthrough Kubernetes API
Init --> Source : fetches selected source and dependencies
Init --> Files : installs and registers environments
Workspace --> Files : edits source; saves executed notebooks
Workspace --> Tasks : Calrissian submits task processes\nthrough Kubernetes API
Tasks --> Shared : mounted task files
Tasks --> S3 : stages inputs / outputs over HTTP
Workspace --> Dask : gateway requests; distributed tasks
note bottom of S3
  Workspace clients also use S3.
  Init configures credentials and initializes buckets.
end note
legend bottom
  C4 container = application/runtime or data store; it does not mean Docker container.
  Kubernetes hosts runtime elements; CLI runs on the workstation.
  This view shows selected relationships. Deployment details are documented separately.
endlegend
@enduml
